# Paths whose modification demands deliberate review, not a reflexive approval.
#
# One path per line, like an allowlist. The text after "#" is the reason shown
# to the reviewer when the tripwire fires, so write it as the thing to look
# for, not a label - "this is sensitive" tells nobody anything they had not
# already assumed. Blank lines and whole-line comments are ignored.
#
# Deliberately not YAML. This is read by a shell script in CI and by a Go test,
# and a format that needs a parser is a format that needs a dependency; the one
# obvious choice for that job, tj-actions/changed-files, is the action that got
# backdoored in 2025 to scrape secrets out of runner logs. grep and cut do not
# have supply chains.
#
# What belongs here is narrower than "important". The test is whether a change
# could remove a safety property WHILE LOOKING ROUTINE IN A DIFF. A deleted
# assertion is three green lines and a smaller file. Things that break loudly -
# a bad provider, a malformed manifest - already fail CI and need no shouting.
#
# tests/go/repo/sensitivepaths_test.go checks this file: every path must exist,
# every path must carry a reason, and every building code must be covered.

tests/go/repo/                              # The building code. Deleting one assertion is a smaller file and a green build.
tests/go/parsed/                            # The one reader the building code reads through, and what keeps it the only way. Loosen it and every guard reads less.
tests/mutations.yml                         # What the mutation ledger admits it cannot prove. Adding a guard here excuses it from ever being shown to fail.
tests/mutations/                            # The proof each guard catches anything, one to a file. Deleting one makes a red check vanish and takes the proof with it.
tests/coverage-blocklist.yml                # Declared debt. Adding a line and bumping the ceiling is two characters and turns a red build green.
tests/languages.yml                         # Which kinds of file anything reads. Moving one to ungoverned: turns off every check for that kind at once.
.github/sensitive-paths                     # This list. Removing a line turns the alarm off for that path, silently.
.github/workflows/                          # Runs with a token. The agent cannot write here, so a human meant this.
.pre-commit-config.yaml                     # Owns formatting and the commit-msg hook, pinned exactly. Unpinning resolves to whatever is latest.

config/management.tpl.json                  # The vault contract. An unwrapped op:// reference reaches a provider as literal text.
modules/infrastructure/cluster/registry.tf            # The invariants that refuse a bad config. Removing one does not fail - it stops refusing.

scripts/details/onepassword/                # Every secret passes here. probe.go returns a Status, never the value it read.
scripts/contractor/internal/phases/health.go    # Gates Migrate, the point of no return. Weakening it reports success over a cluster that never converged.
scripts/contractor/internal/phases/backup.go    # Pipes state into age without plaintext touching disk. Buffering to a file breaks that.
scripts/contractor/internal/phases/restore.go   # The only place that reads the break-glass private key.
scripts/contractor/internal/phases/encryption.go# Sets TF_ENCRYPTION. Wrong here writes plaintext state to a database that ships off-site.
scripts/contractor/internal/phases/sterilize.go # Wipes every secret on exit. Skipping a file leaves secrets on disk and still reports success.
scripts/contractor/internal/phases/teardown.go  # Destroys real infrastructure. The ordering stops state being wiped before the VMs it describes.
scripts/security/                          # Refuses unapproved deliveries and unsigned pushes. Weakening either looks like an ordinary edit.
scripts/details/deliveries/                # Reads the lock guard-deliveries trusts. A parser that skips a section passes every delivery in it unchecked.
scripts/deliveries.lock                     # Every tool installed by hash. One changed hash installs a different file on every lane and workstation, and reads as a regenerated lock.
scripts/take-delivery.sh                    # The only installer the lock reaches. Dropping one hash check installs whatever a supplier serves.
scripts/procurement/                        # Orders the lock, and holds the expedite duty's standing order. Its verbs decide what the estate installs.
scripts/superintendent/                     # Refuses an unsigned push, an unreplayable merge, and a delivery beyond the standing order.
scripts/signedpush/                         # Reads the GitHub App private key. Reaching this mints tokens for this repository.
